  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "sunrise",
      "explanation": "the moment when the sun appears above the horizon; also the time at which this occurs"
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "17596_hinode_ex1",
      "japanese": "{日|ひ}の{出|で}⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{見|み}→見る：00283_miru⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦{山|やま}→山：02168_yama⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦{登|のぼ}った→登る：00660_noboru⟧。",
      "english": "I climbed the mountain to see the sunrise.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "17596_hinode_ex2",
      "japanese": "⟦{今日|きょう}→今日：00496_kyou⟧⟦の→の：09472_no⟧{日|ひ}の{出|で}⟦は→は：00079_ha⟧6⟦{時|じ}→時：09869_ji⟧23⟦{分|ふん}→分：00928_fun⟧です。",
      "english": "Today's sunrise is at 6:23.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "17596_hinode_ex3",
      "japanese": "{初|はつ}{日|ひ}の{出|で}⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦{拝|おが}む→拝む：00328_ogamu⟧⟦ため→ため：01145_tame⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦{早起|はやお}き→早起き：02477_hayaoki⟧⟦した→する：00392_suru⟧。",
      "english": "I woke up early to view the first sunrise of the year.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "JAPANESE CULTURE:\n{初|はつ}{日|ひ}の{出|で} (first sunrise of the new year) is traditionally considered auspicious in Japan. Many people travel to mountains, beaches, or temples to watch the first sunrise on January 1st.\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ⟦{日|ひ}の{入|い}り→日の入り：21211_hinoiri⟧ / ⟦{日没|にちぼつ}→日没：04657_nichibotsu⟧ (sunset)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- ⟦{夜明|よあ}け→夜明け：03655_yoake⟧ / ⟦{明|あ}け{方|がた}→明け方：17595_akegata⟧ (dawn - before sunrise)\n- ⟦{朝日|あさひ}→朝日：23495_asahi⟧ (morning sun)\n- ⟦{日|ひ}→日：02249_hi⟧⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{光|ひかり}→光：01707_hikari⟧ (sunlight)",
